        cache.insert(p, Fetched{...});
        for d in dep_ids { queue.push_back(d); }
    }
    // 纯函数递归组装（cache 已完整，无环风险——Modrinth 依赖为 DAG；
    // 但防环仍需标记：用递归深度限制 32）
    fn assemble(key: &str, cache: &HashMap<String, Fetched>, depth: usize) -> Option<ModRef> { ... }
    assemble(project, &cache, 0).ok_or(...)
}
```

But cache keyed by input project name; deps are project_ids not slugs — cache key must match what we insert: dep.project_id used as key and as fetch key. Modrinth /project/{id_or_slug}/version accepts both, and dependencies give project_id → consistent keys. Root passed as slug → cache[slug]. deps: project_id strings. fetch by id → cache key = the same id string. Works.

Cycle guard: depth limit (e.g., 16) in assemble; if exceeding → treat as leaf (skip). Fine with comment.

