Progress! Download from TUNA mirror succeeded, but extraction didn't find `bin/java`. The TUNA tar.gz extracts to `jdk-21.0.12.1+1/` (the tarball has a top-level dir `jdk-21.0.12.1+1-jre/`), so java is at `dest_dir/<top>/bin/java`, not `dest_dir/bin/java`. For zip (Windows) the same: zip contains top-level `jdk-21.../` folder.

Fix: after extraction, locate the java binary by walking: check dest_dir/bin/java first; if missing, search one level deep subdirectories for */bin/java. Implement a small search:

```rust
fn locate_java_binary(dest_dir: &Path) -> Option<PathBuf> {
    let rel = java_bin_relative();
    let direct = dest_dir.join(rel);
    if direct.is_file() { return Some(direct); }
    // Release archives all come with a top-level version directory
    let Ok(entries) = std::fs::read_dir(dest_dir) else { return None };
    for e in entries.flatten() {
        let candidate = e.path().join(rel);
        if candidate.is_file() { return Some(candidate); }
    }
    None
}
```

Use in resolve_java after extraction (and could simplify find_managed_java which already scans one level). Replace the `let java_path = dest_dir.join(java_bin_relative())` logic with locate_java_binary.

